        code: { lang: 'text', src: "Paschen's law:\n\n  V_breakdown = f(p * d)     only the PRODUCT matters\n\nThe curve is U-shaped:\n\n  LEFT branch  (small p.d):  too few molecules\n                             -> few collisions -> V rises\n  MINIMUM      few hundred volts, most vulnerable\n  RIGHT branch (large p.d):  collisions too frequent\n                             -> energy lost -> V rises\n\nConsequences:\n  partial vacuum is a POOR insulator (near the minimum)\n  hard vacuum is a GOOD insulator (far left branch)\n\nValid for UNIFORM fields.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.2, pp.12-48 (2nd ed. supplied; 5th prescribed)." },
