        topic: 'The Tesla coil',
        slides: [32, 33, 34],
        terms: ['Tesla coil', 'air-cored', 'double tuned', 'high frequency', 'damped oscillation'],
        definition:
          'A Tesla coil is an air-cored double-tuned resonant transformer producing very high voltage at high frequency. A primary capacitor is charged and then discharged through the primary winding by a spark gap, setting up a damped oscillation; the secondary is tuned to the same frequency and accumulates energy over several cycles to reach a far higher voltage. Because there is no iron core there is no saturation, and the high operating frequency, typically tens to hundreds of kilohertz, makes the output unsuitable for power frequency testing but useful for testing at high frequency and for demonstration.',
        takeaway: 'Two tuned air-cored circuits exchanging energy: very high voltage, but at kilohertz, not fifty hertz.',
        visual: 'tesla-coil-energy-exchange',
