        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Marx circuit - parallel charge, series discharge:\n\n  CHARGE:   n capacitors in PARALLEL through high\n            resistances, each to stage voltage V\n            (charging supply need only supply V)\n\n  FIRE:     trigger gap 1\n            -> potential of stage 2 rises\n            -> gap 2 overvolts and fires\n            -> cascade runs up the stack in < 1 us\n\n  DISCHARGE: capacitors now in SERIES\n\n  nominal output = n * V\n  actual  output = eta * n * V     (eta ~ 0.85)\n\nUV irradiation of the gaps improves firing reliability.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.129-142 (2nd ed. supplied; 5th prescribed).' },
