        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Standard impulse CURRENT wave:  8 / 20 microseconds\n\nCircuit: large capacitor bank C\n         discharged through low inductance L\n         and small damping resistance R\n         into the test object\n\n  natural frequency:  omega = 1/sqrt(L*C)\n  peak current:       I ~ V / sqrt(L/C)\n\nINDUCTANCE dominates the front:\n  kiloamperes in microseconds\n  -> conductors short, wide, close together\n  -> minimise the LOOP AREA\n\nDamping: aim for approximately CRITICAL.\n  under-damped -> polarity reversal (not permitted)\n  over-damped  -> front too slow\n\nUsed for: surge arresters, earthing systems.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.143-146 (2nd ed. supplied; 5th prescribed).' },
