        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Chubb-Fortescue peak voltmeter:\n\n  standard capacitor C -> two ANTI-PARALLEL rectifiers\n  moving coil ammeter in ONE branch reads the MEAN current\n\n  charge per cycle in that branch = C * 2 * V_peak\n\n  I_mean = 2 * C * f * V_peak\n\n  ->  V_peak = I_mean / (2 * C * f)\n\nMeasures PEAK, not RMS:\n  - independent of waveform SHAPE\n  - peak is what actually stresses insulation\n\nFails if the waveform has MULTIPLE peaks per cycle.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.7, pp.164-202 (2nd ed. supplied; 5th prescribed).' },
