        definition:
          'Sphere gap readings must be corrected for the state of the air and are sensitive to several practical factors. Sparkover voltage is proportional to relative air density, so temperature and pressure corrections are mandatory. Humidity raises the sparkover voltage slightly because water vapour is mildly electronegative. Dust, pitting or grease on the sphere surfaces lowers and scatters the value, nearby earthed objects distort the field, and inadequate irradiation lengthens the statistical time lag and inflates readings for short impulses.',
        takeaway: 'Correct for air density always; watch humidity, surface condition, proximity and irradiation.',
