        definition:
          'Overvoltages are classified by their origin because origin determines both magnitude and duration, and those two together determine what protection is needed. Lightning overvoltages are the largest, reaching several per unit, but last only microseconds. Switching overvoltages are smaller, typically two to three per unit, and last hundreds of microseconds. Temporary power frequency overvoltages are smaller still, perhaps 1.2 to 1.5 per unit, but persist for seconds, which matters because insulation strength falls as the stress duration lengthens and because arresters cannot absorb energy indefinitely.',
