        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Switching surges:\n\n  closing injects a travelling wave\n  -> REFLECTION at the open far end can DOUBLE it\n  -> TRAPPED CHARGE from a previous opening adds more\n  -> RESTRIKE during opening does the same\n\n  typical 2-3 p.u., worst cases higher\n\nControl measures:\n  1. PRE-INSERTION RESISTORS  - resistance inserted\n     briefly before the main contacts close; damps it\n  2. CONTROLLED CLOSING       - time closure to a\n     voltage ZERO; reduces the injected step\n  3. SURGE ARRESTERS at the line ends for the residual\n\nAbove ~300 kV, SWITCHING surges rather than lightning\nset the insulation level.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.8, pp.251-262 (2nd ed. supplied; 5th prescribed).' },
