        definition:
          'Non-destructive testing establishes the condition of insulation without damaging it, so the same specimen can be tested repeatedly through its service life and its deterioration tracked. The quantities measured are the dielectric constant, which reflects the material and its moisture content, and the dielectric loss, which reflects conduction, polarisation losses and discharge activity. Neither measurement stresses the insulation beyond its normal service level. The value lies less in any single reading than in the trend: a loss factor that has doubled over five years signals deterioration even if its absolute value remains within specification.',
