        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'Transformer impulse test sequence:\n\n  1. REDUCED full wave   (~70%)  <- reference record\n  2. FULL waves          (rated level)\n  3. CHOPPED waves       (rod gap truncates the tail,\n                          steep collapse - most severe\n                          on TURN-TO-TURN insulation)\n  4. REDUCED full wave   (~70%)  <- comparison record\n\nFAULT DETECTION:\n  overlay the NEUTRAL CURRENT oscillograms of shots 1 and 4\n  both at the SAME voltage, so they MUST match\n  ANY difference -> something changed during the\n                    full-level shots -> FAULT\n\nDifference in the LATER oscillations -> changed internal\nresonance -> turn-to-turn short or displaced winding.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.10, pp.339-341 (2nd ed. supplied; 5th prescribed).' },
